1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,630
The most successful night fighter pilot in history survived 164 combat missions and died five years after the war on a country road in France.

2
00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:11,260
His name was Heinz-Wolfgang Schnaufer.

3
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:16,760
He was born in Calw in 1922, where his family ran a wine business.

4
00:00:16,950 --> 00:00:20,330
At 17 he finished school and joined the Luftwaffe.

5
00:00:20,350 --> 00:00:25,230
After training he was posted to the night fighters and flew a Messerschmitt Bf 110.

6
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:29,920
His opponents were the bombers of the Royal Air Force, which attacked German cities by night.

7
00:00:30,010 --> 00:00:36,070
He scored his first victory in June 1942, a Halifax during the raid on Cologne.

8
00:00:36,090 --> 00:00:42,200
He almost always flew with the same crew, radio operator Fritz Rumpelhardt and gunner Wilhelm Gänsler.

9
00:00:42,220 --> 00:00:44,970
In the end all three wore the Knight's Cross.

10
00:00:44,990 --> 00:00:50,090
The Allies called him the Ghost of St. Trond, after his airfield in Belgium.

11
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:54,480
In October 1944 he reported his hundredth victory.

12
00:00:54,500 --> 00:01:00,970
Shortly afterwards, at 22, he became commander of Night Fighter Wing 4, the youngest wing commander in the Luftwaffe.

13
00:01:01,070 --> 00:01:11,470
On 21 February 1945 he was credited with nine Lancaster bombers in a single day, seven of them in the evening within 19 minutes.

14
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:18,510
In total there were 121 victories, almost all four-engined bombers with a crew of seven each.

15
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:23,630
After the war the British put his Bf 110 on display in London's Hyde Park.

16
00:01:23,650 --> 00:01:29,800
A tail fin with all 121 markings is now in the Imperial War Museum.

17
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:34,870
Schnaufer became a British prisoner of war and afterwards took over the family wine business.

18
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,910
In July 1950 he was on a buying trip in France.

19
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:45,420
South of Bordeaux his car collided at a crossroads with a lorry loaded with empty gas cylinders.

20
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:48,080
Two days later he died in hospital.

21
00:01:48,110 --> 00:01:51,470
Heinz-Wolfgang Schnaufer was 28 years old.
